WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Take off a worn-out
robe, put on a new one,

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.180
and you are still you.

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:11.090
The Bhagavad Gita, a Hindu scripture,
uses that very image for death and birth.

4
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.060
Yet most people remember
nothing at all of any past life.

5
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.980
So if you remember nothing of a past life,

6
00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.320
in what sense was it yours?

7
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:25.130
In this mission, you'll compare Hindu
reincarnation with Buddhist rebirth.

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:28.220
Then you'll weigh up
near-death experiences.

9
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:31.360
Can they count as evidence
of life after death?

10
00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:37.150
Your mission: explain in what sense a past
life you cannot remember could be yours.
